      "prompt": "Sprite sheet art, true transparent RGBA, 15 complete poses in 5 columns x 3 rows. Leave a wide transparent margin on the right and left of EVERY character, including both edge columns; no figure touches or crosses any canvas boundary. Place all figures well within a centered 70% wide area of their cells. Full feet and hair visible. Only characters on transparent background: no court/floor/shadow/gradient/hoop, no ball or any other object, no text, no divisions or decorations. Ball is a separate runtime object, entirely absent from drawings. Crisp dark outlines, colorful 1990s arcade pixel illustration.\n\nDorian Mycel exactly matches attached character references in every pose: clean-shaven compact adult human, warm medium-brown skin, dense vivid-purple short curly hair, strong brows, purple Chicago Condas jersey and shorts with silver/lavender trim, dark knee pads, purple wristbands, purple/silver shoes. Two arms, two hands, two legs, two feet. No identity changes.\n\n15 unique right-facing DUNK-WINDMILL animation poses depicting the player sweeping the ball-holding hand in a circular windmill path, then jumping to dunk, with no ball shown. Keep windmill arm close to his body, bent at elbow and never reaching sideways beyond his silhouette: 0 low crouch approach; 1 turns torso, draws arm down; 2 sweeps hand behind hip; 3 arm circles behind body; 4 hand crosses below waist; 5 arm returns to the front; 6 jumps, brings arm up; 7 airborne, arm continues circle; 8 hand rises beside head; 9 peak with bent raised arm; 10 downward finishing motion; 11 follows through; 12 descends; 13 lands in crouch; 14 balanced recovery. Row-major order, same size and identity, full bodies only, ample clear transparent gutters.",
